== D7. chirality wiring: fiber handedness x ledger orientation ==
  triangle ledger: m_hat(sigma=+1) = 0.459889495499, m_hat(sigma=-1) = 0.266653365180
  chiral coupling g = 0.3: commitment rates per cycle:
    L(+1/2) x frustrated     0.023998802866
    R(-1/2) x oriented       0.041390054595
  parity image swaps the pairings: rate asymmetry = 0.017391251729  (PARITY VIOLATED)
  achiral control: relation-free ledger (defect = 0 exactly, one class):
    L and R rates equal by Theorem (P8 Cor 5.2): asymmetry = 0
  -> a parity-violating record coupling requires BOTH ingredients:
     a signed fiber weight (this paper) and a relation-carrying
     oriented ledger (Paper 8).  This is the record Weyl seed, and it
     sharpens clause (vi) of the SM inverse problem.

